WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.410
From the start of Demon Slayer, we are shown
that becoming a demon is basically THE.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:06.410
MOST.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.410
HORRIFIC.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:10.230
THING that can happen to a human.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:15.780
Because even though they gain super strength,
speed, and healing, demons lose every bit

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.570
of their humanity.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:23.689
So when Rengoku rejected the chance to become
a demon during the Mugen train arc, he showed

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:27.300
us that he would rather DIE than become a
demon.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:33.380
But what if Rengoku had decided to live on
and continue fighting as a demon?

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.340
So let’s rewind.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:41.020
Akaza punches a hole through Rengoku’s stomach
and once again offers to turn him into a demon.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:46.180
With Tanjiro screaming in the background,
Rengoku realizes he is going to die.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:51.340
In the original story, Rengoku accepted his
fate with open arms, but let's imagine for

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:56.309
a moment that Rengoku shows some vulnerability
and doesn’t want to die.

00:00:56.309 --> 00:01:02.290
Perhaps he clings onto life with every fiber
of his being, refusing to accept his inevitable

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:03.290
fate.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:08.420
Or maybe he is determined to continue his
fight against demons and is willing to undergo

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.830
the ultimate and painful sacrifice to gain
the power to do so.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:17.450
And so this time, Rengoku accepts Akaza’s
offer.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:22.230
With a wicked smile, Akaza infuses Rengoku
with enough of the demon king’s blood to

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.290
start his transformation into a demon.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:29.250
And while this agonizing process begins, the
sun begins to rise.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:35.210
With his last moments of sanity, Rengoku promises
Tanjiro and the others that he will come back

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:37.790
one day to fight by their side.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:44.880
As the sun rises, Akaza mocks this promise
and then carries Rengoku into the safety of

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:45.880
the dark forest.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:50.840
Now, we know from later on in the manga that
super powerful humans like the Hashira can

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.940
take a few days to fully transform into demons.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:02:00.010
So Akaza takes Rengoku somewhere safe and
isolated during this transformation.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:03.170
Maybe a dark cave or abandoned house somewhere.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:08.750
However, since Akaza selfishly wanted Rengoku
to be his own personal fighting partner, let’s

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:13.470
assume that he does not take Rengoku back
to the demon king, Muzan, and instead keeps

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:18.040
him far enough away that Muzan remains unaware
of Rengoku’s transformation for now.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:23.370
So a few days pass, and the newly formed demon
Rengoku awakens.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:28.340
His body has dramatically transformed with
razor-sharp spikes, terrifying horns, and

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:31.019
swirling flame patterns along his skin.

00:02:31.019 --> 00:02:35.920
And like any new demon, the first thing he
craves is food.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:43.120
And now the possibilities of this insane what
if scenario can branch in many different directions.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:49.010
You see, we already know that demons will
sometimes lose their human memories after

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.010
the transition.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:56.480
So it is possible that Rengoku could completely
forget who he was and become a ruthless evil

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.610
demon who eventually serves Muzan.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:05.900
However, some demons do keep their memories,
or eventually recover them over time, so let’s

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:11.080
assume that Rengoku’s crazy strength and
will enables him to hold onto some of his

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.010
humanity, despite his new demon form.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:18.830
But the cravings that come with his new demonic
form begin to drive him insane.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:23.450
The hunger eats at his insides, and his body
grows weaker by the hour.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:29.049
But Rengoku refuses to give in to his demon
desires and he refuses to eat anything that

00:03:29.049 --> 00:03:30.349
Akaza brings him.

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:37.560
Now Akaza, who thinks that humans are pitiful
and weak, grows increasingly enraged by Rengoku’s

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.209
defiance.

00:03:39.209 --> 00:03:45.420
The air crackles with tension as both Rengoku
and Akaza find themselves eager to fight.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:49.780
Rengoku desires nothing more than to kill
Akaza for revenge, while the other demon is

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:54.209
determined to beat the humanity out of this
new, super strong adversary.

00:03:54.209 --> 00:03:59.879
So they clash, with Rengoku using a brand
new blade of black flames made from his blood

00:03:59.879 --> 00:04:00.879
demon art.

00:04:00.879 --> 00:04:07.030
But despite gaining the usual supernatural
strength, speed, and healing of a demon, Rengoku

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:13.120
struggles to keep up with Akaza's full power,
which he never displayed during the Mugen

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:15.380
train incident.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:20.130
Rengoku fiercely fights against his demonic
cravings for days as Akaza tempts him with

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:21.150
human flesh.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:28.690
The two demons battle each night, and Rengoku's
will to hold onto his humanity weakens.

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:34.190
Akaza warns him that Muzan will kill him if
even thinks about betraying the demons, and

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:38.770
Rengoku knows he can't hide his intentions
from Muzan's mind-reading powers.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:43.280
There is literally nothing Rengoku can do.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:47.560
Except for one thing.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:52.460
Rengoku grows weak from hunger and decides
to end his existence as a demon by stepping

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:53.699
out into the sunlight.

00:04:53.699 --> 00:05:00.520
But just before he can, Akaza tempts him with
more food, and this time, Rengoku’s failing

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.150
spirit snaps.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:06.040
As he indulges his demonic needs, his human
memories fade.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:11.770
They are locked deep within his min and he
eats in order to stay alive.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:15.590
Rengoku’s transformation into a demon is
complete.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:20.669
And now let’s shift to the Demon Slayer
Corps, where Rengoku's betrayal leaves the

00:05:20.669 --> 00:05:22.150
group devastated.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:28.410
And there are many ways that the Demon Slayers
could approach the situation, but no matter

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:35.330
what the loss of one of their strongest warriors
is a terrible blow, made all the worse by

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:38.509
the knowledge that he now serves their greatest
enemy.

00:05:38.509 --> 00:05:42.810
It is likely that Rengoku's father would commit
seppuku in shame.

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:47.080
And we have to imagine that the rest of the
Demon slayers are in chaos.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:52.380
Because from the manga we know that one of
Muzan’s eventual goals is to find the Demon

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:55.380
Slayers’s base and wipe them out.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:06:00.789
Since Rengoku knows where the mansion is,
Kagaya Ubuyashiki, the leader of the demon

00:06:00.789 --> 00:06:05.860
slayers, could be incredibly worried about
Muzan learning this information and he could

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:07.509
consider a few options.

00:06:07.509 --> 00:06:11.410
Such as ordering everyone to leave and set
up a new base somewhere else.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:16.419
Or he may simply think that strengthening
their current base is the best option because

00:06:16.419 --> 00:06:20.990
it is basically already the most demon proof
area in the world.

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:26.389
But let’s assume that for now they choose
to stay, and they have an intense debate about

00:06:26.389 --> 00:06:28.420
what to do regarding Rengoku.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:33.910
Some of the Hashira, like Sanemi, the wind
Hashira, and Giyu, the water Hashira, could

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:36.099
demand they hunt him down for his betrayal.

00:06:36.099 --> 00:06:40.639
Others, like Tanjiro and maybe Gyomei, the
stone Hashira, could argue that they need

00:06:40.639 --> 00:06:44.670
to talk with Rengoku to see if they could
bring him back to their side.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:49.349
And Tanjiro is extremely concerned about what
would happen when the Demon Slayers eventually

00:06:49.349 --> 00:06:50.870
confront Rengoku again.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:55.340
So keep watching to see how this epic clash
turns out later in the video.

00:06:55.340 --> 00:07:00.259
But before the group separates for their next
missions, I definitely think Tanjiro would

00:07:00.259 --> 00:07:05.610
ask permission to go see Lady Tamayo, the
demon who is working on a cure to turn demons

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:10.400
back into people, to see if she has made progress
on the life-changing medicine.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:15.710
But it still probably wouldn’t be ready,
so Tanjiro vows to continue to send her demon

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:17.889
blood to help with the research.

00:07:17.889 --> 00:07:24.720
And with Rengoku now a fully fledged demon,
Akaza would definitely take him to meet Muzan.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:31.689
And wow is the demon king furious with Akaza
for making Rengoku a demon without his permission.

00:07:31.689 --> 00:07:37.419
It is entirely possible that Muzan could obliterate
both of them on the spot, fearing that Regnoku

00:07:37.419 --> 00:07:41.070
may eventually betray him or become too powerful
to control.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:45.840
But for now let’s assume that he restrains
himself because he recognizes the opportunity

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.550
to gather more intel about the Demon Slayer
Corps.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:53.979
Muzan attempts to read Rengoku's mind, but
he is incredibly disappointed that Rengoku

00:07:53.979 --> 00:07:56.350
has lost all of those memories.

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:57.350
For now.

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:01.759
Once more, Muzan’s temper ignites, but he
spares Rengoku’s life for a reason we will

00:08:01.759 --> 00:08:03.610
see later in the video.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:08.550
Because Rengoku was already super strong as
a human, I think Muzan would make him Lower

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:12.460
Moon 1 since that spot is now empty after
the Mugen train battle.

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:14.629
Then Rengoku is sent out into the world.

00:08:14.629 --> 00:08:17.930
And this is where this story gets pretty dark.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:23.159
At this point, the demon Rengoku would be
hungry for power and would likely become a

00:08:23.159 --> 00:08:25.009
terror in the human world.

00:08:25.009 --> 00:08:28.889
He buries his human shame and guilt is deep
alongside his memories.

00:08:28.889 --> 00:08:34.250
His dark flames consume everything in their
path as he rampages through villages.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:40.020
And this takes us to the events of the entertainment
district arc, which we saw in season 2 of

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:41.020
the anime.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:44.890
During this arc, Tanjiro and the others team
up with the Sound Hashira, Tengen, and his

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:48.780
wives to take out the Upper Moon 6 demons
Daki and Gyutaro.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:54.100
And I think these events would progres pretty
much as they did in the original story.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:59.510
Tanjiro and the others investigate and eventually
uncover Daki’s presence.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:03.690
They clash in these epic battles.

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:08.019
Daki is almost killed until Gyutaro reveals
himself.

00:09:08.019 --> 00:09:12.399
And just like in the original, Daki’s ability
to use her cloth as a weapon and Gyutaro’s

00:09:12.399 --> 00:09:15.060
poisonous blades almost wipe out the Demon
Slayers.

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:20.170
But eventually, Nezuko awakens her next demon
form, and in the end, the Demon Slayers are

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:21.269
victorious.

00:09:21.269 --> 00:09:25.740
Though badly injured, the main characters
are still alive, and Tanjiro even briefly

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:29.890
awakened his demon slayer mark during the
fighting.

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:33.880
But now Rengoku enters the fight.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:39.640
You see, after all this time attacking humans
and even practicing against Akaza, Rengoku

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:43.130
has grown extremely powerful.

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:47.070
Much stronger than the Upper Moon 6 demons
who were just defeated.

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:51.920
And so it is the perfect opportunity for Rengoku
to defeat the Demon Slayers and claim Daki

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.650
and Gyutaro’s place within the Upper Moons.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:59.250
And this is a truly awful time for the slayers’
first confrontation with Rengoku.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:02.320
Nezuko is recovering from nearly going Berserk.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:05.730
Tengen and Inosuke are hanging on by a thread.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:10.190
Tanjiro and Zenitsu are completely spent.

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:13.490
But none of that matters to the demon Rengoku.

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:18.290
His black flames begin to consume the town
and burn the people inside.

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:24.430
Exhausted, Tanjiro stands up, wielding his
chipped blade, and confronts this new demon,

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:29.230
but he nearly drops the sword when he recognizes
who has arrived.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:36.740
In utter disbelief, Tanjiro stands frozen,
gazing upon the terrifying demonic form of

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:37.740
Rengoku.

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:41.800
Despite his shock, I still think Tanjiro would
want to talk to Rengoku.

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:46.510
That is after all Tanjiro’s main character
trait, that he always believes in a person’s

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:48.060
capacity to be good.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:53.380
So Tanjiro frantically calls out to Rengoku’s,
begging him to stop the destruction.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:56.290
But Rengoku barely pays him any attention.

00:10:56.290 --> 00:11:01.430
Instead, he heads straight for Tengen, who
is writhing in pain due to the poison still

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:02.589
in his blood.

00:11:02.589 --> 00:11:05.800
Looking down on the Sound Hashira, Rengoku’s
flames flare.

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:11.560
And this might stir memories and guilt within
him, but demon Rengoku is focused on his goals

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.149
and pushes them back down.

00:11:13.149 --> 00:11:17.139
He raises his burning sword, then swipes down
at Tengen.

00:11:17.139 --> 00:11:21.700
Tanjiro leaps forward, raising his sword to
block the killing blow, but the force of the

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:23.400
blow throws Tanjiro aside.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:28.899
Tengen is helpless, and the slash slices through
the Sound Hashira.

00:11:28.899 --> 00:11:33.780
And with one demon slayer dead, this is where
the battle would really heat up.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:39.649
So as we’ve seen with every other demon
Tanjiro has faced, his rage comes spilling

00:11:39.649 --> 00:11:40.649
out.

00:11:40.649 --> 00:11:43.360
Rengoku turns his dark, soulless eyes on the
young Demon Slayer.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:48.339
Tanjiro shouts at his former friend, demanding
that he remember himself.

00:11:48.339 --> 00:11:49.780
Rengoku loved people.

00:11:49.780 --> 00:11:53.600
He wanted nothing more than to protect humans
from demons.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:56.700
But the demon Rengoku barely reacts.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:12:00.350
Instead, he approaches Tanjiro.

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:06.290
With unwavering courage, Zenitsu and Inosuke
stand beside Tanjiro, even though they can

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:11.310
barely move, and together they face down their
most terrifying threat yet.

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:15.410
A former friend turned into a heartless monster.

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:21.440
They clash, but the three of them are definitely
no match for the demon, especially because

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:24.779
they were pushed to the limit in the previous
battle.

00:12:24.779 --> 00:12:28.560
Even Nezuko joins the battle, but she is also
exhausted.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:34.690
So Rengoku traps them in a burning cage of
black flames, and with no shred of humanity

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:39.240
in his eyes, he raises his blade to strike
them down.

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:40.680
Then, the wind picks up.

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:41.720
The flames flicker.

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:44.410
And suddenly, the fire is gone.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.070
And Rengoku vanishes.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:49.830
At least as far as the three young demon slayers
can tell.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:51.360
Sword clashes ring out.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.600
Bursts of flame and wind stir the street.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:55.690
The sound of gushing water surrounds them.

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:57.940
And suddenly, everything stops.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:02.810
On one end of the street, stands the demon
Rengoku, blood dripping and cuts healing.

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:07.970
In front of Tanjiro stands Giyu and Sanemi,
the Water and Wind hashiras, breathing hard.

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:11.220
And these two would not just show up randomly.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:15.040
I think it is entirely possible that they
would have been hunting Rengoku this whole

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:18.610
time, and have just now caught up to the former
hashira.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:22.540
So Giyu looks back at the boys and would probably
order them to flee.

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:28.360
But Sanemi cares less about them, and stares
down at the burnt corpse of Tengen and his

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:30.080
rage boils over.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:31.910
He shouts at Rengoku, cursing him.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:35.430
Now that they’ve tracked him down, they
are going to end him.

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:41.190
Rengoku smirks, flames rising around him,
and the battle resumes.

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:48.360
Zenitsu would probably ask if they should
flee, but Tanjiro and Inosuke would not even

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:53.810
respond as they strain to keep up with the
incredible display of power in front of them.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:58.470
And we know from later in the story, that
the Upper Moon one, two, and three demons

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:02.779
are pretty far above the power levels of the
individual Hashira.

00:14:02.779 --> 00:14:07.730
And while Rengoku hasn’t quite reached that
level yet, he is certainly much stronger than

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:10.480
anything that the Hashiras have faced before.

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:13.839
So this definitely isn’t going to be an
easy battle.

00:14:13.839 --> 00:14:19.940
However, Giyu and Sanemi are two of the strongest
Hashira and together they manage to keep Rengoku

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:21.380
occupied.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:25.399
The sun is coming soon, so they must stay
alive until it arrives.

00:14:25.399 --> 00:14:28.650
As the battle continues, the town burns.

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:29.779
Screams fill the air.

00:14:29.779 --> 00:14:34.660
And the Hashira are distracted by trying to
keep the innocent people alive.

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:40.829
Meanwhile, Rengoku delights in the chaos,
causing more destruction with his flames.

00:14:40.829 --> 00:14:44.550
Amidst the burning town, Tanjiro finds himself
torn.

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:49.560
He knows that he is outmatched in a battle
of this level, but he cannot just stand by

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:51.740
and watch his friend’s perish.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:57.320
And despite it all, he refuses to give up
hope that Rengoku can still be saved.

00:14:57.320 --> 00:14:59.120
But time is ticking away.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:04.000
In the blink of an eye, Giyu is engulfed in
flames, and Sanemi’s attempt to save him

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.410
earns him a wicked slash across his leg.

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:09.870
The two Hashira stumble, and Rengoku charges
towards them.

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:14.040
The battle begins again, but the Hashira are
clearly losing their grip.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:20.320
And I think it’s at this point that Tanjiro
would not be able to hold himself back.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:25.180
As always, when he is most desperate, Tanjiro
finds the next level of strength.

00:15:25.180 --> 00:15:30.350
Tanjiro’s heart races as he feels the rhythmic
power of sun-breathing filling his body.

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:35.190
Giyu cuts Rengoku across the chest, but flames
explode from the wound, stunning the water

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:36.190
hashira.

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:39.370
Rengoku grabs Giyu by the throat and squeezes
tightly.

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:44.720
Giyu gasps, his neck bulging, but suddenly
Giyu is free and Rengoku’s severed hand

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:46.339
falls to the ground.

00:15:46.339 --> 00:15:49.040
Tanjiro stands over a breathless Giyu.

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:53.220
His demon mark flares on his forehead, giving
him the strength to fight.

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.220
As always, when Tanjiro is most desperate
he finds the next level of strength.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:58.839
Rengoku grins, blocking a blow from Sanemi
and then coming after Tanjiro.

00:15:58.839 --> 00:16:00.959
But Tanjiro is furious.

00:16:00.959 --> 00:16:08.370
The rage fuels his muscles and he leaps forward
so quickly Rengoku can barely block the strike.

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:11.649
Together, the three demon slayers rain blows
on their former friend.

00:16:11.649 --> 00:16:15.769
With each strike, Tanjiro shouts memories
at Rengoku.

00:16:15.769 --> 00:16:17.590
Reminding him of their treasured time together.

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:18.839
How he laughed with them.

00:16:18.839 --> 00:16:20.319
How he trained them.

00:16:20.319 --> 00:16:22.820
How he was willing to give up his life for
them.

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:28.750
The memories fuel Tanjiro’s spirit, but
nothing seems to break through to Rengoku.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:32.660
But Tanjiro keeps trying because this demon
was his friend and I don’t think he would

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:33.800
ever give up on him.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.449
But Tanjiro is slowing.

00:16:36.449 --> 00:16:39.440
Exhausted, he slips, and gets tossed to the
side.

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:41.480
Giyu and Sanemi are quickly downed as well.

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:45.639
They simply cannot keep up with the stamina
and recovery of this overpowered demon.

00:16:45.639 --> 00:16:49.740
So Rengoku stands over them, ready to deliver
the final blow.

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:52.000
But Tanjiro rises again.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:53.000
His sword is gone.

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:54.329
His breaths are heavy.

00:16:54.329 --> 00:16:55.720
His sun-breathing flares.

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:58.029
And he stares the demon in the eye.

00:16:58.029 --> 00:17:00.780
And he does the only thing that he can.

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:03.860
Tanjiro yells Rengoku’s name.

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:06.620
Over and over again, he repeats it.

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.860
Trying to reach down and awaken the buried
memories.

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:15.970
Because just like his sister, Nezuko, Tanjiro
has to believe that the human is still inside

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:18.790
of this terrifying demon.

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:22.089
And with each word, Rengoku eyes grow unfocused.

00:17:22.089 --> 00:17:23.760
The flaming sword lowers.

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:27.569
And suddenly tears form in the dark pits of
his eyes.

00:17:27.569 --> 00:17:29.690
And a word forms on his lips.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:30.690
“Tanjiro.”

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:31.690
The flames falter.

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:34.429
Sanemi goes for another strike, but Rengoku
blocks it.

00:17:34.429 --> 00:17:35.429
“Sanemi.”

00:17:35.429 --> 00:17:38.780
His gaze turns to Giyu and he calls the Water
Hashira’s name as well.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:42.549
And then Rengoku, the former flame Hashira,
drops his sword.

00:17:42.549 --> 00:17:47.541
He stares at his hands, tears running down
his face, as he looks at the Demon Slayers

00:17:47.541 --> 00:17:48.630
in front of him.

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:50.470
Tanjiro has reached him.

00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:51.610
His memories return.

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:56.110
But so do the shame and guilt that he has
buried all this time.

00:17:56.110 --> 00:18:00.340
And with Rengoku finally coming back, there
are a few ways that this could go.

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:03.850
If he is truly returned, the demon slayers
could bring him back with them.

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:08.881
However, as we saw with Sanemi when he first
met Nezuko, when a demon kills a human, some

00:18:08.881 --> 00:18:12.870
Hashira believe there is forgiving that sin.

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:18.450
So while emotions overwhelm Rengoku, Sanemi
goes for a death strike, but Tanjiro steps

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:19.450
in front.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:23.100
He kneels before Rengoku and tells him that
he can still choose to come back.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:25.570
He can still choose to do good, but Rengoku
doesn’t believe him.

00:18:25.570 --> 00:18:29.840
His eyes turn to Tengen’s burnt body, and
his cries grow even louder.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:32.270
And he simply asks Sanemi to end him.

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:38.230
And the wind hashira is more than willing,
until a haunting laugh echoes down the dark

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:39.230
street.

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:42.010
Muzan has arrived.

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:46.100
Because while Muzan was initially disappointed
he couldn’t get information about the Demon

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:50.750
Slayers when they first met, he probably knew
that at some point Rengoku would regain those

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:51.750
memories.

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:55.120
So he was just waiting all this time.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:59.640
And With Rengoku’s memories returned, Muzan
reads Rengoku’s mind, and finally learns

00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:04.820
the secrets of the Demon Slayer Corps, including
where to find their base.

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:06.380
The demon slayers rise.

00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:09.410
Tired and ragged, they face down the demon
king.

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:15.580
Muzan applauds Rengoku for being so useful,
and then he calls the former Hashira to his

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:16.580
side.

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:20.190
He tells Rengoku that he can use that guilt
and shame to grow stronger.

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:23.909
But Rengoku doesn’t listen.

00:19:23.909 --> 00:19:24.909
Instead he rises.

00:19:24.909 --> 00:19:30.062
He begs everyone to flee, reminding them that
the sun is rising, and Muzan can’t stay

00:19:30.062 --> 00:19:31.150
here long.

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:35.520
Muzan scowls, and tries to trigger the curse
that will instantly kill Rengoku.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.890
But it doesn’t work.

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:40.690
With his memories fully returned, and his
humanity with it, Rengoku’s connection to

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:43.150
Muzan has been severed.

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:47.470
Now we know that Muzan is insanely powerful.

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:52.789
Way more powerful than even the Upper Moon
demons, so it is possible that he kills all

00:19:52.789 --> 00:19:54.179
of them right here.

00:19:54.179 --> 00:19:58.980
But to continue the story, let’s assume
that with the sun close to rising, Rengoku

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:00.670
stands to face the demon king.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:01.920
He tells the others to run.

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:05.380
And without hesitation, Giyu and Sanemi take
the others and flee.

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:12.350
And let’s assume that Rengoku can hold him
off for at least a short while before Muzan

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:14.909
eventually ends the former flame hashira’s
life.

00:20:14.909 --> 00:20:19.421
And with the sun rising, the Demon Slayers
manage to retreat safely to the Demon Slayer

00:20:19.421 --> 00:20:20.750
Corps base.

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:25.261
Despite the heart-wrenching tragedy of losing
Tengen and Rengoku for a second time, there

00:20:25.261 --> 00:20:26.659
is no time to rest.

00:20:26.659 --> 00:20:31.000
With Muzan now aware of their location, it
would only be a matter of time before the

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:34.610
demons launch an all out assault on the Demon
Slayer Crops.

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:39.750
And this insane, all-out battle will require
Tanjiro and the other Demon Slayers to summon

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:45.500
every ounce of strength, skill, and courage
they possess just to survive.

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:49.840
But one thing we do know is that Tanjiro will
never give up protecting his friends, so he

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:54.440
would certainly unlock his full potential
to defeat the demon king or die trying.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:58.470
And if you want to watch my full breakdown
of why this part of his character makes Tanjiro

00:20:58.470 --> 00:21:02.460
a fantastic great protagonist, you can click
right here.

00:21:02.460 --> 00:21:03.529
Thanks for watching.

